REGENT OF KEPAHIANG

PROVINCE OF BENGKULU

REGIONAL REGULATION OF KEPAHIANG REGENCY NUMBER 10 OF 2016

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

AGAINST ACTS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

THE REGENT OF KEPAHIANG,

Considering : a. that every citizen has the right to survival, to grow and develop, to obtain protection of personal self, honor and dignity as a complete human being in family, community, national and state life;

b. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence and discrimination;

c. that all forms of acts of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination;

d. that violence against women and children in Kepahiang Regency continues to increase in both quantity and quality, thus requiring efforts of prevention, protection, recovery and law enforcement;

e. that laws and regulations concerning the protection of women and children victims of violence require the support of regulations and institutional mechanisms at the Kepahiang Regency level that can guarantee their implementation;

f. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, letter d and letter e, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation of Kepahiang concerning the Protection of Women and Children Victims of

Violence;

